+# Room capability maps (2026-07-07; reviewed 2026-11-03)
 
-A comprehensive reference map for every room — *everything the room is supposed to offer*. Built in the same format as the Discovery Studio capability map (which lives with the guardian specs, being the most strictly-specified room). These are the **binding mind contract** the wire-to-production build runs against (`deliverables/plans/antaeus-wire-to-production-plan-2026-07-07.md`): every wired room's Pass-1 (Mind & Capability Fidelity) walks its map line by line.
+These maps describe each room's purpose, capabilities, state meanings, handoffs, and design constraints. They were reviewed during language remediation. Current source code and the certification evidence in `docs/language-remediation-2026/` determine implemented behavior; older plans and screenshots are historical references, not authority to restore obsolete wording or unsupported capabilities.
 
-Each map: 1·Purpose · 2·What it offers (the full capability table) · the room's distinctive structure (movements / verdicts / fronts / segments / streams / lanes / cues, as applicable) · N·Flows (in / out) · N·Guardrails (must-never-be-flatten | what-it-is-NOT). Compiled from canon §4.x + shipped `src/<room>` + reconciled to current doctrine.
+Preserve useful visual distinctions, ordinary sales terminology, and explicit operator judgment. Explain what each score measures, which inputs support an assessment, and what an action does. Label sample data, uncertain inferences, and forecasts accurately. A branded room name must be accompanied by a clear function. Internal schema keys and technical component names may remain stable without becoming customer-facing labels.
 
-Banned-word occurrences are confined to the "Banned on the face" documentation tables (the per-room language teardowns) — reference usage documenting what the *product* may not say, exactly as the Discovery map documents "Proof threshold."
+Tables marked `data-copy-context="deprecated-example"` retain migration examples of language the product must reject. Those examples are historical comparisons, not wording recommendations. Other text is active implementation guidance and must follow the governing rule: “Antaeus may have a point of view. It may not require translation.”
 
