-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Cold Call Studio · Live Instrument · capability map</div><h1>Walk into the cold call ready. Log what happened after.</h1><div class="fam">Live Instrument (live execution) · settled 2026-07-06 (the game plan · prep-before / log-after)</div><p>Help the seller walk into a cold call ready — the opener, the pain to find, how to show it’s real, the ask, and the pushback they’re likely to hit — and capture what happened after. It <b>prepares</b> the call and <b>logs</b> the result; it does not ask the seller to operate the app during the call. A cold call is wildly unpredictable — the seller can’t follow a clock or click buttons mid-call.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.9 (no-live-call-operation, 2026-07-04) + shipped src/cold-call-studio. Settled design: cold-call-studio-gameplan-2026-07-06.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">A <b>prep surface + an after-the-call capture surface</b>, never a during-call console. The seller reviews the shape and the likely branches beforehand so they walk in with conviction, makes the call, and logs the outcome after. Won by walking in prepared, not by reading a screen mid-call.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The call’s shape</div><h2>The ordered steps (reviewed beforehand)</h2><div class="sd">Each part carries the pushback a buyer is likely to give, with a line ready for it.</div><table><tr><th style="width:26px">#</th><th>Step</th></tr><tr><td><span class="n">1</span></td><td><b>Get ready</b></td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">2</span></td><td><b>Open</b></td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">3</span></td><td><b>Find the pain</b></td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">4</span></td><td><b>Show it’s real</b></td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">5</span></td><td><b>Ask for the meeting</b></td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">6</span></td><td><b>Wrap up</b></td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The call’s shape</b></td><td>The ordered steps (above), reviewed before the call.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Likely-pushback branches</b></td><td>Each step’s probable brush-off with a ready line.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The get-ready checklist</b></td><td>The pre-flight before the seller walks in.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>After-call outcome capture</b></td><td>meeting booked · callback · referral · voicemail · rejected · hung up · no answer.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The plain after-call read</b></td><td>what went well / what to sharpen next time.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The log of recent calls</b></td><td>The running record of outcomes.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>account + what’s happening from <b>Signal Console</b></li><li>who to call (the person + their role)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>on a booked meeting → <b>creates a Deal</b> (into Deal Workspace)</li><li>call outcomes → <b>Dashboard</b> · <b>Deal Workspace</b> · <b>Readiness</b> · <b>Handoff Kit</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Language — plain, mid-sales-legible</div><h2>The user is the seller</h2><div class="sd">Banned on the face: thread · loom · pull · pressure · proof · say-next · call memory · “the move.” The user is the <b>seller</b> (or <i>you</i>), never “rep.”</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The deal-creation on a booked meeting</li><li>The prep-then-capture shape</li><li>The live consequence of a real call</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a script library</li><li>Never a during-call clicker</li><li>Not a live-call console</li><li>Not a dialer</li></ul></div></div></div>
