-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Dashboard · Command Chamber · capability map</div><h1>The one ranked object under the most pressure — and the one move.</h1><div class="fam">Command Chamber (ranking) · settled 2026-07-04</div><p>Show the operator the single ranked object under the most pressure right now, with one dominant next move, <b>without browsing</b>. The Dashboard is where the operator stops choosing between modules and starts being told which deal, signal, or pilot to act on first — it ranks everything under pressure, explains why a specific object came up first, and offers one compressed act-or-inspect move.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.2 + the command-intelligence engine (Part V · buildCommandObjects / rankCommandObjects / summarizeCommandContext / explainCommandObject). Settled design: dashboard-CHOSEN-complete-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Replace the hallway (equal-weight doors) with a smarter front door: one ranked object, one dominant move, the reasoning shown. Three density modes support different cognitive states; all three keep the ranking. This is the room the whole system’s workspace-health summaries flow into. <b>Supersession (2026-07-08, founder-confirmed):</b> the settled 2026-07-04 "command + standing cockpit" folds the three cognitive states into one surface (standing = the Brief read · the one move = Spotlight · skip-the-board = Queue), so there is no explicit mode switcher, and the "this week&#39;s reads" card is not carried on the Dashboard. Sections 2 + the "this week&#39;s reads" row below are retained as history.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The three density modes</div><h2>Brief / Spotlight / Queue — same ranking, different cognitive state <span style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12px;font-weight:400;color:var(--ink-3)">— superseded 2026-07-08, folded into the cockpit</span></h2><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Mode</th><th>Shape</th><th>For the operator who…</th></tr><tr><td><b>Brief</b></td><td>A 2–5 sentence narrative read + one variable-insight line</td><td>wants the morning read in prose, then the one move</td></tr><tr><td><b>Spotlight</b></td><td>The single focal object at depth + a ranked “next” rail</td><td>wants to act on the top object and see why it’s first</td></tr><tr><td><b>Queue</b></td><td>A ranked triage list — rank prefix + reason chips per row</td><td>wants to work down the pressure list one at a time</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>Everything the room does</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ranked object list</b></td><td>Everything under pressure, ranked — deals, signals, pilots, moves, the ICP itself, system reads.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Brief narrative</b></td><td>A deterministic morning read (buildBriefNarrative) naming the spotlight, the queue composition, the ranking confidence, the runner-up.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Spotlight focus object</b></td><td>The dominant card: family kicker + serif title + the “why this is here / why this order” reasoning + one orange primary CTA + 0–2 ghost secondaries.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Queue triage flow</b></td><td>The counter-style ranked list; click a row to re-spotlight.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ranking inputs (shown, never hidden)</b></td><td>how hot the signals are on an account · how much pressure a deal is under · how stale · dollar value · what changes downstream if you act.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Readiness anchor</b></td><td>A single topbar anchor — the maturity verdict label + chevron; click opens the Readiness drawer as an overlay (no route change).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The “this week’s reads” card</b> <span class="pill retired">superseded</span></td><td>Retired from the Dashboard 2026-07-08 (the cockpit does not carry it). The workspace-scope observations still live in the Briefing’s Workspace stream.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Graph reward + workspace-health summary</b></td><td>Compounding shown as real state change — never decorative scores.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · The ranking engine</div><h2>How the order is decided</h2><div class="sd">The command-intelligence engine builds command objects from every room’s snapshot, ranks them, and explains the order. Family priority breaks ties.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Family</th><th style="width:80px">Priority</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td><b>risk</b></td><td>5</td><td>deal-room pressure (top_pressure entries)</td></tr><tr><td><b>advisor / opportunity</b></td><td>4</td><td>advisor asks · signal/outbound moves</td></tr><tr><td><b>move</b></td><td>3</td><td>the next outbound / discovery move</td></tr><tr><td><b>icp</b></td><td>2</td><td>fires when accounts/signals/deals exist but no ICP</td></tr><tr><td><b>system</b></td><td>1</td><td>dependency warnings the system raises</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>workspace-health summaries from <b>every deep room</b></li><li>the system-health variant from <b>Readiness</b> + <b>Quota Workback</b></li><li>signal heat from <b>Signal Console</b> (<span class="mono">gtmos_signal_room_health</span>)</li><li>deal pressure from <b>Deal Workspace</b> (<span class="mono">gtmos_deal_workspace_health</span>)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>one-click routing into whichever room owns the ranked object — with <span class="mono">focusObject</span> + <span class="mono">returnTo</span> preserved</li><li>the Readiness drawer overlay (verdict + gating evidence)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The whole-motion standing leads the room (the verdict masthead) · one dominant move under it · the standing row where each part is a door <span style="color:var(--ink-3)">(the cockpit; supersedes the Brief/Spotlight/Queue modes, 2026-07-08)</span></li><li>The room-browsing rail does not belong center stage</li><li>The ranking must keep showing its reasoning — never reduced to decorative scores</li><li>One dominant move per surface</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Not a dashboard of vanity metrics</li><li>Not a grid of equal-weight boxes</li><li>Not a hallway of module doors</li><li>Not a BI report</li></ul></div></div></div>
