ives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Seven authored sections</b></td><td>Evidence-based prose that explains observed patterns and their limitations to another seller.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Per-section status</b></td><td>ready / partial / empty, with incomplete sections and evidence limits visible.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The per-section cross-workspace assessment</b></td><td>The “one thing to notice” — an assessment combining evidence from multiple workspaces.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The open-book reader</b></td><td>A two-pane bound reader: contents + readiness on the left plate, one authored part in full reading serif (Newsreader) on the right page.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Section-readiness count</b></td><td>A recessive “N of 7 parts ready” segment bar — never the hero.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The share-link mechanic</b></td><td>Read-mode workspace access for an external email — the persistent sharing control.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ceremony hook</b></td><td>Triggers the existing visual transition on the first upward Readiness transition into Runnable with founder support.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · The ceremony moment</div><h2>Sales handoff readiness improves</h2><div class="sd">When Readiness transitions UP from <b>Partially documented → Runnable with founder support</b> for the first time in a workspace, show the existing visual transition (not a toast): an animated reveal — the verdict change, the kit count moving (e.g. 2/7 → 4/7), a serif headline (“Sales handoff documentation is ready to review”), and a one-time CTA to share the workspace read-mode. Once per workspace per upward transition; downward transitions are silent.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><d