-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Outdoors Events · Live Instrument · capability map</div><h1>Where people are gathering, found for you.</h1><div class="fam">Live Instrument (live execution) · ADR-015 + ADR-016 · settled 2026-07-07 (proximity + the get-there rail)</div><p>A discovery surface that finds offline gatherings relevant to the operator’s product category and surfaces them — the Signal Console pattern applied to events instead of accounts. The system finds; the operator marks, prioritizes, dismisses. <b>Informational, not attributional</b> — no ROI tracking, no deal-attribution. The operator shouldn’t be the one googling for conferences.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.22 + ADR-016 (discovery reframe, supersedes ADR-015 §3/§6) + ADR-015 (room mind) + the 2026-07-07 get-there utility. Settled design: outdoors-events-icon-rail-2026-07-07.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Read the workspace’s product category, run web-search-grounded queries for gatherings in that space + adjacent + indirect, and return events with real source URLs and a one-sentence relevance reason. The operator’s attention goes to <b>deciding which events matter</b>, not finding them. This is the Briefing pipeline pattern: workspace context → web search → LLM enrichment → typed rows → voice-gated surfacing.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The relevance tiering</div><h2>Proximity as the organizing axis</h2><div class="sd">The tiering is felt as distance, not flat labels — an orange→blue→grey gradient on the proximity spine.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Tier</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td><b>Direct</b></td><td>your category — closest in</td></tr><tr><td><b>Adjacent</b></td><td>your buyers — one ring out</td></tr><tr><td><b>Indirect</b></td><td>their orbit — the outer ring (your ICP might show up)</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The discovery console</b></td><td>“Run discovery now” + the last-run summary (status · events written · cost · relative time).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The event record</b></td><td>name · kind · where · dates · status · tags · notes · source URL · relevance_tier · relevance_reason · discovered_at · source_kind · dedupe_key.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The status lifecycle</b></td><td>watching → planning → attending → attended → passed → archived.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The discovery run ledger</b></td><td><span class="mono">outdoors_events_runs</span> — cost + search-count + status per sweep.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The audit envelope</b></td><td>per discovered event — where did this event come from?</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The get-there rail</b></td><td>per-row live weather (Open-Meteo, keyless) + one-tap flights / hotels / register / add-to-calendar.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The manual “add by hand”</b></td><td>A demoted secondary affordance for a private invite the system missed.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · The get-there boundary</div><h2>Outbound links + a weather glance only</h2><div class="sd">Once the scout finds a gathering worth the time, the room helps the operator <b>decide and depart</b> — but it hands off to the real sites (Google Flights / hotels / the registration page / an .ics) and <b>never stores or manages an itinerary</b>. Registration is a link out, never registration tooling built in-room. This honors the “never a logistics tracker” rule. New travel/weather/conference line-icons (plane · bed · sun/cloud/rain · lanyard-badge · calendar · pin · ticket) join the brand iconography.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="sd">On-demand discovery only (no weekly cron, founder direction 2026-06-02). Cost ceiling per workspace; degradation policy (warning 80%, throttle 100% drops adjacent + indirect, pause 150%).</div><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li><span class="mono">workspace_profile.product_category</span> (the seed for the query plan)</li><li>web sources via the Anthropic web_search tool</li><li>(no reads from other Antaeus rooms in first-ship — category-anchored)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>deferred:</b> Phase 2 — Prospecting Desk handoff (event-tagged contacts → prospects)</li><li><b>deferred:</b> Phase 3 — Signal Console attribution + Deal Workspace sourced-from tag</li><li>a navigation-only chip on the Briefing’s World view (no data flow)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The discovery posture (the operator does not author events — the system does)</li><li>The relevance tiering (Direct / Adjacent / Indirect is the organizing axis)</li><li>The voice gate on every LLM-authored string</li><li>The audit envelope chain (where did this event come from?)</li><li>The get-there layer as outbound links + a weather glance, never itinerary management</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>No deal-attribution</li><li>No registration tooling built in-room</li><li>Never an event-aggregator feed</li><li>Never a CRM screen or a logistics tracker</li></ul></div></div></div>
