o’s hands-on, sized to the deal — headcount lives only here.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Who’s-missing prompts</b></td><td>“Someone from IT” / “a day-to-day driver” with an inline find-them → name-them + ask-the-champion-for-an-intro flow.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The adoption meter</b></td><td><i>actually using it</i> (of the people you enrolled, how many are active) + <i>actions taken</i> — fed from the product’s own usage or marked by hand.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Gated per-check-in steps</b></td><td>A step unlocks only when the prior is done.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Share kit</b></td><td>A collapsible library to drive adoption + arm the champion: getting-started video · per-role quick-starts · case study · “why you’re in this pilot” note · champion kit · kickoff announcement · FAQ · reference-customer intro.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The Mutual pilot plan</b></td><td>You + the champion agree the goal, steps, and results meeting — co-owned, a shared action, not a solo template.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The write-up</b></td><td>The short document the champion carries to their boss.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>the deal from <b>Deal Workspace</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>pilot state + risk into <b>Deal Workspace</b></li><li>the stop rule into <b>Future Autopsy</b></li><li>portable evidence into <b>Call in a Favor</b></li><li>pilot state into <b>Handoff</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Language — the plain-words eradication</div><h2>No foundry, no “proof”</h2><div class="sd">The old room was a foundry metaphor drenched in banned words — all eradicated on the face. Code enum keys may stay; no user ever sees the banned word.</div><table data-copy-context="deprecated-example"><tr><th style="width:260px">Banned on the face</th><th>Say instead</th></tr><tr><td>proof · cast · mold · forge/foundry · ingot · heat/heat-ledger · kill rule · readout</td><td>the pilot · the results · the evidence</td></tr><tr><td>the quality band</td><td>ready / almost ready / more detail required</td></tr><tr><td>the mold grid</td><td>the parts of the pilot</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The guide (never a scorecard or checklist)</li><li>Adoption as the success meter (never the outcome number alone)</li><li>The people / multi-threading layer (right-sized, never “get everyone”)</li><li>The who’s-missing prompt</li><li>The feel-of-ease (never a wall of fields)</li><li>The Share kit + Mutual pilot plan</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a scorecard</li><li>Never a checklist</li><li>Never a wall of fields</li><li>Not a metrics dashboard</li></ul></div></div></div>
