r><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Quality score + what’s-missing</b></td><td>How complete an account is + what still needs answering.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The three-question confirm</b></td><td>The guard step (above).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Who-to-target guidance</b></td><td>Rides the active focus — “go for the VP of RevOps who owns the forecast, not the junior rep who fills the CRM.”</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The stage lifecycle</b></td><td>just added → confirmed → ready → sent, + set-aside-with-reason; counts per stage.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Territory Architect</b> — focus/division, tier, approach vocabulary + who-to-target</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>confirmed accounts → <b>Signal Console</b></li><li>a ready account → <b>Outbound Studio</b> (first message)</li><li>carries focus + approach context forward</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The honesty of the search — Antaeus runs its OWN web research, cited (never claim a vendor/Sales-Nav feed it doesn’t have)</li><li>Confirm as a real step (accounts pass the three questions before Signal Console)</li><li>Who-to-target guidance</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a filing cabinet</li><li>Never a “pretend search”</li><li>Not a Sales Navigator integration</li><li>Not a bought-list importer</li></ul></div></div></div>
