>The target the whole room works backward from.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Typical deal size (ACV → benchmark band)</b></td><td>SMB / Mid-Market / Enterprise / Strategic — sets which benchmark the believability read tests against.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Win rate + cycle length</b></td><td>The conversion + timing inputs.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The conversion assumptions</b></td><td>Advanced / gated — the funnel arithmetic, recessive.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The derived daily habit</b></td><td>messages & calls a day · first meetings a week · real opportunities & deals a quarter.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The believability read</b></td><td>“this plan is a stretch — one assumption is optimistic” + what it costs. A plain judgment, never a bare score.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Pipeline coverage</b></td><td>From Deal Workspace — ratio vs the band target, weighted vs raw, the dollar gap.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The pace projection</b></td><td>Projected year-end landing vs target + the need-vs-actual scoreboard for a returning seller.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>pipeline from <b>Deal Workspace</b> (coverage)</li><li>logged motion from <b>Outbound</b> / <b>Cold Call</b> (the pace/actuals read)</li><li>onboarding targets</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>targets into the <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>coverage truth into <b>Readiness</b></li><li>execution pressure (the daily habit) into <b>Outbound</b> + <b>Cold Call</b></li><li>the daily/weekly cadence into <b>Founding GTM</b> §7 (day-one operating rhythm)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Language + open rename</div><h2>Plain, no funnel jargon</h2><div class="sd">Th