-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Readiness Score · System Ledger · capability map</div><h1>Could a real first-hire walk in tomorrow and run the motion?</h1><div class="fam">System Ledger (synthesis) · design settled 2026-07-07 (the climb)</div><p>Answer one question — <b>is the system inheritable yet?</b> — and give the operator a verdict, not a number. Readiness is a <b>maturity assessment</b>, not a pressure rail: an integral over time, not a derivative. The Dashboard already answers “what should I act on today?”; Future Autopsy answers “what’s decaying?”; Readiness answers “is the workspace inheritable yet?”</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.17 + the readiness engine (verdict.ts · dimensions.ts · dashboard readiness-aggregator). Settled design: readiness-score-climb-2026-07-07.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Give the operator a single truth about inheritability, prominent but never obnoxious — anchored on the Dashboard topbar at all times. The room shows the <b>verdict</b>, the gating evidence behind it, and what would change the verdict next. Internal dimension scoring stays as the math; the operator never sees a “/20” or the word “dimension.”</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The five verdicts</div><h2>Gate-based, not threshold-based</h2><div class="sd">Verdicts are present-evidence gates, not score thresholds. Each gate uses the internal 5-part × 20 math but the face names the <b>state</b>, never a number.</div><table><tr><th style="width:215px">Verdict</th><th>What it means</th><th>Gate (internal)</th></tr><tr><td><b>You are the system</b></td><td>Founder-led, no transferable surface yet</td><td>any part at 0</td></tr><tr><td><b>Building</b></td><td>Activity exists but a hire would still be improvising</td><td>≥2 parts ≥8, none ≥16</td></tr><tr><td><b>Inheritable with guardrails</b></td><td>A hire could run it with you there to answer questions</td><td>every part ≥10 AND ≥1 part ≥16 AND first pilot evidence exists</td></tr><tr><td><b>Hire-ready</b></td><td>The motion would survive a 2-week founder vacation</td><td>every part ≥14 AND closed-won exists AND Future Autopsy run AND ≥1 actionable pilot</td></tr><tr><td><b>Hire-ready, repeatable</b></td><td>Multiple wins, losses analyzed, advisors lit, kit composed</td><td>all Hire-ready + win/loss ≥1 AND advisors ≥1 AND handoff ≥5/7 ready</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>Everything the room does</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The verdict</b></td><td>The dominant serif state name + a plain one-line read of what a hire could / couldn’t do today.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The gating evidence</b></td><td>The specific present-evidence checks behind the current verdict.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>“What would move the verdict next”</b></td><td>Plain, prescriptive unlocks — the exact things that flip the next gate.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The climb (the ladder over time)</b></td><td>The five levels as a vertical ladder — passed levels sit behind in <b>forest green</b> (“left behind 3 weeks ago”), the current level is “you are here,” the next is the goal + “what it takes.”</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The five parts of the motion</b></td><td>Demoted to quiet ready/thin chips (forest = solid, amber = thin) — your targeting · your outreach · your discovery · your open deals · your pilot evidence. Never bars, never scores.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Internal dimension scoring</b></td><td>5 parts × 20 = 100, kept for the gate math only — never surfaced as a number.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The topbar anchor + single-fold drawer</b></td><td>Verdict label + chevron on the Dashboard topbar → opens an overlay drawer (no route change).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The read-only “share with a hire”</b></td><td>The one durable move — read-mode workspace access for an external email.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Ceremony hooks</b></td><td>Fires the Founding GTM set-piece on a verdict transition UP.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>summaries from <b>every deep room</b> (cloud-synced via data-client.ts, not the legacy snapshot key)</li><li>deal-health vitals from <b>Deal Workspace</b></li><li><b>Pilot Desk</b> outcomes</li><li><b>Future Autopsy</b> run history</li><li>advisor deployment outcomes from <b>Call in a Favor</b></li><li>section-readiness count from <b>Founding GTM</b> (drives the repeatable gate)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>verdict + topbar anchor into the <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>a verdict transition <b>UP</b> fires the ceremony moment in <b>Founding GTM</b></li><li>verdict + gating evidence into the <b>Welcome</b> read</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Language — plain, no scoring vocabulary</div><h2>Scrubbed on the face</h2><div class="sd">The shipped Phase-5.A drawer leaked internal scoring language + retired nouns — all scrubbed.</div><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Banned on the face</th><th>Say instead</th></tr><tr><td>“proof”</td><td><b>pilot evidence</b></td></tr><tr><td>“sanity-check”</td><td><b>with you there to answer questions</b></td></tr><tr><td>naked “dimension”</td><td>name the actual <b>part of the motion</b> (your targeting / outreach / discovery / open deals / pilot evidence)</td></tr><tr><td>“/20” or a bare score</td><td>the <b>state</b> — never a number</td></tr><tr><td>“verdict” (courtroom sense)</td><td>stays internal engine name only; the face names the state itself</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Verdict as gate-based truth (not threshold-based)</li><li>The singular question (hire-ready or not)</li><li>The ceremony at verdict transitions UP</li><li>The climb — readiness felt as an integral over time</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never duplicate what the Dashboard says about “what’s weakest now”</li><li>Never a 5-bar score breakdown as the primary surface</li><li>Not a pressure rail</li><li>Bars are decoration — the verdict is the value</li></ul></div></div></div>
