-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Settings · Trust Annex · capability map</div><h1>Your workspace is safe. Here’s how to keep it that way.</h1><div class="fam">Trust Annex (utility) · settled 2026-07-07 (the safe deposit)</div><p>Keep the user safe, make trust and recovery real, without stealing attention from live operating rooms. Open with a plain reassurance — “your workspace is safe, it’s saved to the cloud as you work, not trapped on this laptop” — then the controls to take a copy, restore, or erase it, then the quiet preferences and account controls. Calm, plainspoken utility with a <b>hierarchy</b>: data safety leads; preferences and account recede.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.20 (the safe-deposit redesign + language teardown, 2026-07-07) + shipped src/settings. Settled design: settings-safe-deposit-2026-07-07.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Make trust + recovery real without operating-room energy. The redesign fixed a real drift (the pre-arc 9-card grid): the dual-export confusion is resolved, account controls were added, and demo mode is tucked. Data safety is the point of the room, so it leads.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · What it offers</div><h2>The three sections, in order</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The trust statement</b></td><td>where your data lives + signed-in-as + last-saved reassurance — the serif hero with a forest “your workspace is safe” kicker.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Your data (the dominant section)</b></td><td>Download my workspace (one durable cloud copy) · Restore from a file · Delete everything (behind a type-to-confirm gate) · an Advanced disclosure for the device-offline copy.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>How the app works for you</b></td><td>what you sell (discovery-framework category) · how-much-the-app-explains (density) · let-the-system-suggest (the Phase-F toggle) · try-a-sample (demo).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Your account</b></td><td>signed-in-as · Sign out · re-run onboarding · Privacy · Terms.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The drift it fixed</div><h2>What was wrong before</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Drift</th><th>The fix</th></tr><tr><td>Two overlapping exports the app had to apologize for</td><td>one “Download my workspace” (durable cloud); device-offline copy demoted to Advanced</td></tr><tr><td>Internal-architecture language as copy</td><td>scope kickers (WORKSPACE-LEVEL / BROWSER-ONLY / ACCOUNT-LEVEL) + DB jargon (cloud rows, browser cache) — all gone</td></tr><tr><td>Retired nouns in the delete copy</td><td>“proofs” → pilot evidence; no “advisor deployments”</td></tr><tr><td>Missing account controls</td><td>added Sign out + Privacy / Terms</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>the <span class="mono">gtmos_*</span> localStorage keys + the cloud workspace</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>manages those keys + the cloud workspace (download / restore / delete)</li><li>bridges to Supabase auth (sign-in / sign-out)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The trust signals (the plain “your workspace is safe” reassurance, the honest delete)</li><li>Data-safety as the room’s dominant billing (never buried among preferences)</li><li>The account controls (sign out, privacy/terms)</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never mixed with operating-room energy</li><li>Never internal-architecture language as copy</li><li>Not a 9-card grab-bag</li><li>Not a fake-excitement product surface</li></ul></div></div></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><div class="ct">Language and capability review · 2026-11-02</div><div class="cb">Use the current source and docs/language-remediation-2026 for implementation. Earlier design references below preserve history; they do not authorize deprecated customer language or capabilities that the source does not implement. Keep stable internal identifiers separate from display wording. Distinguish evidence, assessment, forecast, and recommendation.</div></div>
+  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Settings · workspace settings · capability map</div><h1>Manage workspace data and preferences.</h1><div class="fam">workspace settings (utility) · settled 2026-07-07 (the safe deposit)</div><p>Settings explains storage and connection status, export and restore scope, deletion scope, activity capture, preferences, and account controls. State what each operation actually covers.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.20 (the safe-deposit redesign + language teardown, 2026-07-07) + shipped src/settings. Settled design: settings-safe-deposit-2026-07-07.html.</div></div>
+  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Keep data controls easy to find and accurately describe their scope. A verified cloud connection is not proof that every record is synchronized. Avoid promises of complete backups or deletion unless the operation covers the entire workspace model.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · What it offers</div><h2>The three sections, in order</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Storage and connection status</b></td><td>where your data lives + signed-in-as + last-saved reassurance — the serif hero with a forest “workspace storage status” kicker.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Your data (the dominant section)</b></td><td>Export supported cloud records, restore from a file, or delete the documented record groups after confirmation. Explain retained records, row limits, and partial failures. Keep the device copy separate.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>How the app works for you</b></td><td>what you sell (discovery-framework category) · how-much-the-app-explains (density) · let-the-system-suggest (the Phase-F toggle) · try-a-sample (demo).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Your account</b></td><td>signed-in-as · Sign out · re-run onboarding · Privacy · Terms.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The drift it fixed</div><h2>What was wrong before</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Drift</th><th>The fix</th></tr><tr><td>Two overlapping exports the app had to apologize for</td><td>one “Download my workspace” (durable cloud); device-offline copy demoted to Advanced</td></tr><tr><td>Internal-architecture language as copy</td><td>scope kickers (WORKSPACE-LEVEL / BROWSER-ONLY / ACCOUNT-LEVEL) + DB jargon (cloud rows, browser cache) — all gone</td></tr><tr><td>Retired nouns in the delete copy</td><td>“proofs” → pilot evidence; no “advisor deployments”</td></tr><tr><td>Missing account controls</td><td>added Sign out + Privacy / Terms</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>the <span class="mono">gtmos_*</span> localStorage keys + the cloud workspace</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>manages those keys + the cloud workspace (download / restore / delete)</li><li>bridges to Supabase auth (sign-in / sign-out)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The trust signals (the plain “workspace storage status” reassurance, the honest delete)</li><li>Data-safety as the room’s dominant billing (never buried among preferences)</li><li>The account controls (sign out, privacy/terms)</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never mixed with operating-room energy</li><li>Never internal-architecture language as copy</li><li>Not a 9-card grab-bag</li><li>Not a fake-excitement product surface</li></ul></div></div></div>
