+  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Signal Console · execution workflow · capability map</div><h1>Monitor account signals and priority.</h1><div class="fam">execution workflow (live execution) · protected room · settled 2026-07-04 (Attention Router)</div><p>Signal Console stores watched accounts and supporting signals, then ranks them using signal type, credibility, and age. Review those inputs before recommending outreach.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.7 + the heat engine (shipped src/signal-console) + ADR-006 (substrate role). Settled design: signal-console-attention-router-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
+  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Explain account priority using current signals and recorded activity. Preserve the ranking math and data contracts. Research is useful when it supports a specific account decision; do not infer buyer intent or urgency merely from a score.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The account-priority engine</div><h2>How an account ranks</h2><div class="sd">Priority is computed, not stored — the source of truth is the signals + their timestamps.</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Priority score = signal count × type weight × source credibility × recency decay</b></li><li>Bands (the Attention Router): <b>act now</b> · <b>reach while warm</b> · <b>emerging</b> · <b>going cold</b> — the relevance is felt as a band, not a bare number</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The account list</b></td><td>The named accounts being watched — sorted by where attention should go.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Signal records</b></td><td>Time-limited events attached to each account.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Priority score per account</b></td><td>The computed rank (above) — feeds Dashboard command ranking.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The morning brief</b></td><td>A daily summary of watched-account signals.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Research posture</b></td><td>Distinguish accounts with enough context for outreach from accounts that still need research.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The workspace-health block</b></td><td>compounding vs still weak.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The enrich-all flow</b></td><td>Refresh signals, firmographics, and account-priority inputs for watched accounts.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Add-account</b></td><td>By hand or from Prospecting Desk enrichment.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>accounts from <b>Prospecting Desk</b> + <b>Territory Architect</b></li><li>ICP-Match score from <b>ICP Studio</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>ranked accounts → <b>Outbound Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call Studio</b> · <b>LinkedIn Playbook</b></li><li>account priority + available evidence → <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>account priority + activity state → <b>sales handoff documentation</b></li><li>accounts + signals → the <b>Briefing</b> (read-only data source per ADR-006)</li><li>act-on handoffs → <b>Outbound</b> · <b>Discovery Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call</b> · <b>Deal Workspace</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Signal interpretation</li><li>Connect account research to a concrete outreach or monitoring decision</li><li>Account priority meaning</li><li>A protected room — may not be made generic, renamed, or folded in</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a badge list</li><li>Never a passive timeline</li><li>Not a notification feed</li><li>Not a static account directory</li></ul></div></div></div>
