 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Deal Workspace · Diagnosis Table · capability map</div><h1>Which deals will close-lost if you do nothing this week.</h1><div class="fam">Diagnosis Table (intervention) · settled 2026-07-04</div><p>Surface the recovery queue — which deals are weakest, why, and what the next corrective move is. The room is an <b>intervention board, not a Kanban</b>. First-fold exposes pressure fast: which deals will close-lost if I do nothing this week, and what’s the smallest corrective move. Stage is not truth unless next-step truth backs it up.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.13 + the recovery-ranking + 9-field health engine (shipped src/deal-workspace). Settled design: deal-workspace-toggleable-views-2026-07-04.html (Focus / Timeline / List).</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Lead with pressure. The recovery ranking (staleness + next-step pressure + close-date pressure) sorts every deal into a lane and names the smallest corrective move. Stage truth is only truth when a real dated next step backs it.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The recovery lanes</div><h2>Where the work is decaying</h2><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Lane</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td><b>Critical</b></td><td>will close-lost this week without a move</td></tr><tr><td><b>At-risk</b></td><td>decaying — a corrective move is due</td></tr><tr><td><b>Healthy</b></td><td>backed by a real dated next step</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The 9-field deal-health modal</div><h2>What backs the stage</h2><div class="sd">Stage is not truth unless these back it up.</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>champion</b> · <b>economic buyer</b> · <b>use case</b> · <b>pain</b> · <b>competition</b> · <b>decision process</b> · <b>notes</b> · <b>forecast</b> · <b>momentum</b></li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The intervention board (dealGrid)</b></td><td>The recovery queue — weakest first, each with its cause + smallest corrective move.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The 9-field deal-health modal</b></td><td>The qualification truth behind each deal (above).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The recovery queue panel</b></td><td>The ranked “act on this or lose it” list.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The deal-health panel</b></td><td>The per-deal vitals read.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The loss-reason modal</b></td><td>Captured on transition to lost — feeds Playbook loss patterns.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The toggleable views</b></td><td>Focus / Timeline / List — different reads on the same pressure.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>deals auto-created from <b>Cold Call</b> (on meeting_booked)</li><li>deal state updates from <b>Discovery Studio</b></li><li>pilot state from <b>Pilot Desk</b></li><li>advisor effect from <b>Call in a Favor</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>deal pressure into <b>Future Autopsy</b> · <b>Dashboard</b> · <b>Readiness</b> · <b>Handoff Kit</b></li><li>loss patterns into <b>Founding GTM</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Deal pressure</li><li>Next-step quality</li><li>Stage truth (backed by a real next step)</li><li>Qualification seriousness</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a passive record page</li><li>Not a Kanban board</li><li>Not a pipeline CRM view</li><li>Not a stage-column drag surface</li></ul></div></div></div>
