 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">LinkedIn Playbook · Live Instrument · capability map</div><h1>LinkedIn as disciplined air cover — never the opening scene.</h1><div class="fam">Live Instrument (live execution) · settled 2026-07-06 (the one move)</div><p>Use LinkedIn as disciplined air cover — never the opening scene. Public cue first, ask only when trust has compounded. The inbox is not where you start: the five cues run <b>watch public signal → comment with one operating read → connect after recognition → give-first → ask only when it’s warranted</b>.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.10 + the motion engine + 5-cue ladder (shipped src/linkedin-playbook). Settled design: linkedin-playbook-one-move-2026-07-06.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Show the single next public-first move on the hottest account already lit in Signal Console / Outbound — one account at a time. Channel-specific discipline: the ask is the last cue, not the first.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The five-cue ladder</div><h2>Where you are on the account</h2><table><tr><th style="width:26px">#</th><th style="width:180px">Cue</th><th>What it is</th></tr><tr><td><span class="n">1</span></td><td><b>Watch</b></td><td>watch a public signal</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">2</span></td><td><b>Comment</b></td><td>comment with one operating read</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">3</span></td><td><b>Connect</b></td><td>connect after recognition</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">4</span></td><td><b>Give-first</b></td><td>give value before asking</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">5</span></td><td><b>Ask</b></td><td>ask only when it is warranted</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The five-cue ladder</b></td><td>The where-you-are spine on the account (above).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The cue log form</b></td><td>Log the cue that was run + its outcome.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The cue-method templates</b></td><td>Connection · Public cue · Give-first · Ask — ready-to-paste scaffolds.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Channel memory stats</b></td><td>touches · acceptance · reply rate — the compounding read on the channel.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The one ready-to-paste move</b></td><td>The single next public-first move for the hottest account.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>account + persona from <b>Signal Console</b> / <b>Outbound Studio</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>motion truth → <b>Dashboard</b> · <b>Signal Console</b> · <b>Readiness</b> · <b>Handoff</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Channel-specific discipline (public cue first, ask last)</li><li>The one move at a time</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never generic outreach tips</li><li>Not an inbox-first outreach tool</li><li>Not a connection-request blaster</li><li>Not a content scheduler</li></ul></div></div></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><div class="ct">Language and capability review · 2026-11-02</div><div class="cb">Use the current source and docs/language-remediation-2026 for implementation. Earlier design references below preserve history; they do not authorize deprecated customer language or capabilities that the source does not implement. Keep stable internal identifiers separate from display wording. Distinguish evidence, assessment, forecast, and recommendation.</div></div>
+  <div class="mast"><div class="k">LinkedIn Playbook · execution workflow · capability map</div><h1>Plan LinkedIn outreach alongside calls and email.</h1><div class="fam">execution workflow (live execution) · settled 2026-07-06 (the recommended action)</div><p>LinkedIn Playbook recommends an account-specific action from recorded signals, connection requests, messages, and outbound activity. It does not infer trust from activity counts.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.10 + the motion engine + 5-cue ladder (shipped src/linkedin-playbook). Settled design: linkedin-playbook-one-move-2026-07-06.html.</div></div>
+  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Preserve the five actions and their logging. Recommend the next action from recorded interaction state, and make templates specific to the account. Acceptance and reply statistics describe the sample; they do not establish universal success thresholds.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The five LinkedIn actions</div><h2>Where you are on the account</h2><table><tr><th style="width:26px">#</th><th style="width:180px">Cue</th><th>What it is</th></tr><tr><td><span class="n">1</span></td><td><b>Watch</b></td><td>watch a public signal</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">2</span></td><td><b>Comment</b></td><td>comment on a specific relevant observation</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">3</span></td><td><b>Connect</b></td><td>review prior interaction before connecting</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">4</span></td><td><b>Give-first</b></td><td>give value before asking</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">5</span></td><td><b>Ask</b></td><td>ask only when it is warranted</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The five LinkedIn actions</b></td><td>The where-you-are spine on the account (above).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The cue log form</b></td><td>Log the cue that was run + its outcome.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The cue-method templates</b></td><td>Connection · Public cue · Give-first · Ask — ready-to-paste scaffolds.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Channel memory stats</b></td><td>touches · acceptance · reply rate — the summary of recorded channel outcomes.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The recommended LinkedIn action</b></td><td>The single next public-first move for the highest-priority account.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>account + persona from <b>Signal Console</b> / <b>Outbound Studio</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>recorded activity → <b>Dashboard</b> · <b>Signal Console</b> · <b>Readiness</b> · <b>Handoff</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Channel-specific discipline (public cue first, ask last)</li><li>The one move at a time</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never generic outreach tips</li><li>Not an inbox-first outreach tool</li><li>Not a connection-request blaster</li><li>Not a content scheduler</li></ul></div></div></div>
